      "content": "The immediate priority is to stop the temperature rise, which you should do by moving the container to a location with ambient cooling or attempting to engage any auxiliary cooling systems if available. You must immediately notify your shipping line and the consignee, as this is a major incident requiring a documented chain of custody. For safety verification, you need to monitor the internal temperature continuously and, once the shipment arrives, conduct a thorough quality assessment, including testing for microbial load, following HACCP guidelines. Do not allow the tuna to be sold until a qualified food safety expert has signed off on its viability.",
